{
  "title": "Routine serum globulin information improves cross-cycle prediction of log CRP beyond albumin and white-cell count",
  "abstract": "In complete-case NHANES adults aged 20\u201379, adding continuous serum total-protein-minus-albumin to a frozen spline model containing albumin, white-cell count and demographic/metabolic measures reduced MEC-weighted log-CRP MSE from 1.086310 to 1.049520 in separately sampled 2007\u201308 participants after fitting in 2005\u201306; gain 0.036790, target-PSU conditional-source 95% interval [0.022986, 0.050653]. This is cross-cycle surrogate prediction, not new biomarker discovery or independent clinical-cohort validation.",
